{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"1. Uh, Yeah. You're right. I definitely don't want per work tree scoping. My point being still stands, though. I do think we probably want per branch scoping. Does that make sense? Like, I understand that this point of, like, the current system is not per branch stored, but is per branch shown or accessible or viewed or something, but I'm just suspicious of that. I feel like it would just be simpler and safer to do per branch storage in my opinion.\n2. I do agree that making export reachability aware by default is something that would be an improvement, but I'm not convinced that we can't or shouldn't just switch to actually making storage branch specific as well or instead. Like, that feels like the actual cause of the problem and just making export reachability aware just kinda papers over the problem with a Band Aid solution. At least that's the vibe I'm getting. I see how it looks like that is woodwork as a general solution. It looks like it from our current use cases. But I I don't just want to work from our current use cases. I suspect that we will have more use cases later. And I don't know that every one of those use cases will want to use the export command. I suspect some may just find that they need to read directly, um, if our export command is not up to snuff. But I'm not... I I don't know. Is is that a reasonable, uh, critique, or do you think export is literally just exported? Like like, it is all it needs to be. I I I I don't know. It feels wrong to me.\n3. Yeah. Again, I didn't actually mean per work tree. I think I meant per branch that entire time. Like, per branch is the actual unit that I would care about. \n- What if... I feel like the problem with this that we're running into is that just notes aren't made, like references, notes, whatever these are, aren't made for what we're doing. What if we just created a tiny Git repo inside the h